#: hivepress-trust-signals.php:871
msgid "Signals"
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-trust-signals.php:872
msgid "Choose which signals appear and tune the response statistics thresholds. A signal only shows when its data exists, so an enabled signal can still be hidden on some pages."
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-trust-signals.php:877
msgid "Enabled signals"
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-trust-signals.php:878
msgid "A signal is hidden automatically when its extension is inactive or there is not enough data - omitted rather than estimated. The response thresholds are set below."
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-trust-signals.php:886
msgid "Response rate grace period (hours)"
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-trust-signals.php:887
msgid "Conversations newer than this are left out of the response rate, so a brand-new unanswered message does not lower a vendor's rate unfairly. Default: 48."
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-trust-signals.php:896
msgid "Minimum response rate to display (%)"
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-trust-signals.php:897
msgid "The response rate is only shown at or above this percentage, so a low rate is never advertised. Set to 0 to always show it. Default: 80."
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-trust-signals.php:906
msgid "Slowest response time to display (days)"
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-trust-signals.php:907
msgid "Hides the response time signal when a vendor's typical first reply is slower than this many days. The displayed wording always comes from the true value, so it reads true at any setting. Default: 3."
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-trust-signals.php:916
msgid "Minimum conversations"
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-trust-signals.php:917
msgid "Response time and rate are only shown once a vendor has received at least this many conversations."
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-trust-signals.php:928
msgid "Removing the Plugin"
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-trust-signals.php:935
msgid "Deleting this plugin keeps your settings and each vendor's accumulated activity figures, so a reinstall carries on where it left off. WordPress's own delete-screen warning about data loss is generic and does not apply unless you tick the box below. Switching the plugin off never removes anything."
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-trust-signals.php:940
msgid "Delete All Data"
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-trust-signals.php:941
msgid "Delete everything when this plugin is deleted"
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-trust-signals.php:947
msgid "With this ticked, deleting the plugin also removes every setting on this page, each vendor's completed bookings total and the recorded last-active times. The bookings total only ever counts up and cannot be rebuilt, and nothing asks you to confirm at the time. Leave it unticked to keep everything."
msgstr ""

